#### File Class

Standard Definition

The File class in Java (from java.io package) represents a file or directory (folder) in your computer system. It
provides methods to create, delete, rename, check existence, get size, and more - but it doesn't deal with the
content inside the file.

package com.FileHamdling.BufferReader_Writer;

import java.io.File;

public class Demo1 {
	public static void main(String[] args) {
		String path1 = "C:\\Users\\Saurav Kumar\\OneDrive\\Documents\\JAVA\\FileHandling\\input.txt";
		File file = new File(path1);
		System.out.println(file.canRead());
		System.out.println(file.canWrite());
		System.out.println(file.canExecute());
		System.out.println(file.getAbsolutePath());
		System.out.println(file.isFile());
		System.out.println(file.isDirectory());
	}
}

